// A function may hold at most 256 basic blocks, because JirFunction stores
// them inline. Past the cap the compiler used to hand back block 255 -- one
// already in use -- so an `if` could end up with its then-block and its
// end-block being the same block. The branch then had two identical targets
// and the loop's back-edge landed inside its own body, and the program spun
// forever with nothing reported. It is a hard error now (JDA-C007).
